        <p>When tracking multi-sport high school talent in the region, consistency and high-stakes speed are the key variables. On our scouting radar this week is standout athlete <strong>Isaiah Brown</strong>—known natively across his athletic programs as <strong>"Zay."</strong></p>

        <p>Brown displays a rare tier of physical intelligence, moving across two distinct competitive high school programs. He has logged varsity execution for both <strong>BHS</strong> and the <strong>Lutheran West Longhorns</strong>. Maintaining high-impact production across a relentless football, basketball, and track schedule marks him as an elite multi-athlete, but it's his pure spring sprint tracking that jumps off the analytics sheet.</p>

        <div class="quote">
            "We recently verified Zay scorching a spectacular 49-second finish in the 400-meter dash. Breaking sub-50 as a high schooler is an elite athletic baseline, displaying an explosive vertical burst that opposing defenses struggle to mirror on the field."
        </div>

        <div class="school-panel">
            <h4>Verified Prospect Board:</h4>
            <p>• <strong>Programs Logged:</strong> BHS & Lutheran West High School<br>
            • <strong>Track Profile:</strong> 49s (400m PR)<br>
            • <strong>Creative Alias:</strong> Recording under the artist handle Z4YR</p>
        </div>

        <p>What makes his layout unique is that his creative drive doesn't pause when the game clock hits zero. Off the field, he operates under the moniker <strong>Z4YR</strong>, translating that same rhythmic focus and cadence into a growing catalog of melodic trap releases. Our scouting report shows the same exact focus: whether he's breaking angles on the gridiron or locking down loops in the lab, Zay is built to win.</p>

